title: President Ebert must appoint a new government!
subtitle: Our military buildup has caused sanctions from France and other countries.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1925 and month >= 1
max-visits: 1

= President Ebert must appoint a new government!

The December 1924 elections produced a divided Reichstag and the current Chancellor, Wilhelm Marx, has thus far proved unable to find a majority. We must decide which course to take to restore a stable government.

- @appointment_menu: Let us begin.

@appointment_menu

- @luther: Hans Luther (I), in a five-party coalition (This is the historical option.)
- @marx: Refuse to dismiss Marx (Z), the current Chancellor
- @alternative: Let us attempt to find an alternative Chancellor.

@luther
on-arrival: chancellor = "Luther"; chancellor_party = "I"; right_coalition = 1; DNVP_in_government = 1; foreign_minister = "Stresemann"; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister = "Schiele"; interior_minister_party = "DNVP"; justice_minister = "Frenken"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister = "Brauns"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister = "Gessler"; reichswehr_minister_party = "DDP"; economic_minister = "Neuhaus"; economic_minister_party = "DNVP"; finance_minister = "Schlieben"; finance_minister_party = "DNVP"; agriculture_minister = "von Kanitz"; agriculture_minister_party = "I";

We agree to appoint Hans Luther as Chancellor, even though it means the reactionary DNVP entering government. Our Left Wing are outraged by this action.

@marx

Our refusal is all well and good but Marx has been unable to form a viable coalition for the past month. We must find a viable pathway forward.

- @grand_coalition: Pressure Marx to form a Grand Coalition including the SPD.
- @toleration: Provide SPD votes to prop up a minority Bourgeois coalition.
- @article_48: Invoke Article 48 and rule by decree
- @appointment_menu: Let Marx’s government fall and consider an alternative chancellor.
- @let_it_fall_new_elections: Let Marx’s government fall and fresh elections be held.

@grand_coalition

Despite our pressure, the DVP is reluctant to enter a grand coalition. How will we overcome their objections?

- @stresermann: DVP leader Gustav Stresermann led a Grand Coalition as Chancellor before – perhaps he will again?
- @bluff: Threaten to call snap elections if the current Reichstag cannot form a stable government.
- @bluff2: Threaten to invoke Article 48 and rule by decree.
- @appointment_menu: This isn’t working. Let Marx’s government fall and consider an alternative Chancellor.

@toleration

Despite our pressure, the SPD is reluctant to enter into such an arrangement. How will we overcome their objections?

- @bluff3: Threaten to call snap elections if the current Reichstag cannot form a stable government.
- @bluff4: Threaten to invoke Article 48 and rule by decree.
- @concessions2: Offer concessions to the SPD.
- @gessler: Suggest Otto Gessler of the DDP as a more acceptable choice for Chancellor
- @grand_coalition: Offer a Grand Coalition instead.
- @appointment_menu: This isn’t working. Let Marx’s government fall and consider an alternative Chancellor.

@article_48
choose-if: never
unavailable-subtitle: President Ebert is unwilling to take such action until all other paths fail.

@let_it_fall_new_elections
choose-if: never
unavailable-subtitle: President Ebert is unwilling to call fresh elections so soon after the last ones.

@stresermann
on-arrival: chancellor = "Stresermann"; chancellor_party = "DVP"; spd_in_government = 1; in_grand_coalition = 1

The DVP agree and a new Grand Coalition is formed under Stresermann.

go-to: election_1928.ministries

@bluff
choose-if: never
unavailable-subtitle: The DVP know that President Ebert is unwilling to call fresh elections so soon after the last ones.

@bluff2
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; in_grand_coalition = 1

The DVP fold and agree to form a Grand Coalition under Marx.

go-to: election_1928.ministries

@bluff3
choose-if: never
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD have little to lose from fresh elections.

@bluff4
choose-if: never
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD finds this no worse than toleration.

@alternative
go-to: election_1928.coalition_menu

@concessions2
on-arrival: spd_toleration = 1 

The SPD finally agrees and a minority coalition is formed under Wilhelm Marx.

@gessler
on-arrival: chancellor = "Gessler"; chancellor_party = "DDP"; spd_toleration = 1; foreign_minister = "Stresemann"; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister = "Külz"; interior_minister_party = "DDP"; justice_minister = "Marx"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister = "Brauns"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister = "Gessler"; reichswehr_minister_party = "DDP"; economic_minister = "Curtius"; economic_minister_party = "DVP"; finance_minister = "Luther"; finance_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister = "Haslinde"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"

The SPD finally agrees and a minority coalition is formed under Otto Gessler.

